    <section class="oop-section">
        <h2 class="oop-section-title">Concept Overview</h2>
        <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 1.5rem;">
            <li><strong>Stack (LIFO)</strong>: Last In, First Out. Like a stack of plates. Use `append()` and `pop()`.</li>
            <li><strong>Queue (FIFO)</strong>: First In, First Out. Like a lunch line. Use `append()` and `pop(0)`.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="oop-section">
        <h2 class="oop-section-title">Common Misconceptions</h2>
        <div class="info-content">
            <p><strong>1. `pop(0)` vs `pop()`</strong></p>
            <p>For Queue, removing the <em>first</em> item is `pop(0)`. Removing the last (Stack) is `pop()`. If they swap them, the tests will fail.</p>
            
            <p><strong>2. `peek()` errors</strong></p>
            <p>Checking the top/front without removing. Must handle empty lists (return None) to avoid `IndexError`.</p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="oop-section">
        <h2 class="oop-section-title">Solution Code</h2>
        <div class="code-block" style="background: #1e1e1e; color: #d4d4d4; padding: 1rem; border-radius: 6px; overflow-x: auto;">
            <pre><code>class Stack:
    def __init__(self):
        self.items = []

    def push(self, item):
        self.items.append(item)

    def pop(self):
        if not self.items: return None
        return self.items.pop()  # Removes last

    def peek(self):
        if not self.items: return None
        return self.items[-1]

class Queue:
    def __init__(self):
        self.items = []

    def enqueue(self, item):
        self.items.append(item)

    def dequeue(self):
        if not self.items: return None
        return self.items.pop(0)  # Removes first</code></pre>
